# No Git Commits or Pushes

## Never run these without being explicitly told to:
- `git commit`
- `git push`
- `git push --force`
- `gh pr create`
- Any command that writes to the remote repository

## What to do instead
Make the code changes, then stop. Tell the user what files were changed and let them handle git.

```
// ❌ NEVER — committing/pushing without being asked
git add . && git commit -m "fix: ..." && git push

// ✅ CORRECT — stop after code changes
"Done. Changed app/api/projects/[id]/materials/upload/route.ts — push when ready."
```

## If the user asks you to commit AND push
Only do what they literally asked for. "Commit this" means commit only — not push.
"Commit and push" means both — but confirm before pushing to main/master.
